    <div class="container-fluid p-3 info-container">
      <div class="intro text-center">
        <h1>What is Far Reach Co?</h1>
        <hr>
      </div>

      <section>
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Far Reach Co.</strong> is a <strong>free, collaborative virtual tabletop and campaign management platform</strong>
          designed for tabletop RPG communities. Built by a small team of friends who wanted to play D&D together despite being far apart,
          Far Reach Co. prioritizes simplicity, accessibility, and keeping players immersed in their adventures.
        </p>
      </section>
      <br>

      <section>
        <h2>Core Features</h2>

        <h3>Virtual Tabletop (VTT)</h3>
        <p>
          A <strong>platform-agnostic virtual tabletop</strong> with real-time collaboration.
          Fast, simple, and uncluttered - allowing you to focus on the story rather than the software.
          Supports images, drawing, and token management. Create personal tables from your dashboard or
          campaign-specific tables within Wyrlds.
        </p>

        <h3>D&D 5E Character Sheets</h3>
        <p>
          Custom character sheet management with a fresh and intuitive approach.
          Create and manage character sheets from your personal dashboard, then link them to specific
          campaigns (Wyrlds) to share with your gaming group.
        </p>

        <h3>Wyrlds - Private Campaign Environments</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Wyrlds</strong> are private, enclosed campaign environments where Game Managers can organize
          their adventures. Within a Wyrld:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Players link their character sheets to the campaign</li>
          <li>Game managers create virtual tables specific to that Wyrld</li>
          <li>Set permissions and privileges for players to control tables</li>
          <li>All records, images, and calendars are encapsulated within that Wyrld</li>
          <li>Shared resources stay within the private campaign space</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Your main dashboard remains your personal workspace for creating tables and records that belong only to you,
          while Wyrlds provide collaborative spaces for your gaming groups.
        </p>

        <h3>D&D 5E SRD Reference</h3>
        <p>
          Complete System Reference Document with <strong>1340+ monsters, spells, classes, races, equipment, and more</strong>.
          Quick reference guide designed for fast lookup during gameplay.
        </p>

        <h3>Records System</h3>
        <p>
          Create and manage lore, notes, monster stat blocks, and other campaign resources.
          Personal records stay in your dashboard, while Wyrld records are shared with your campaign group.
        </p>
      </section>
      <br>

      <section>
        <h2>Who Built It?</h2>
        <p>
          Far Reach Co. was created by a small team of <strong>musicians, artists, developers, and teachers</strong>
          who came together through their love of storytelling and tabletop RPGs. What started as tools for
          their own gaming group has grown into a platform for the wider TTRPG community.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/about-us">Read our full story →</a>
        </p>
      </section>
      <br>

      <section>
        <h2>What Makes It Different?</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Free to use</strong> - No paywalls or subscriptions</li>
          <li><strong>Platform-agnostic VTT</strong> - Works with any TTRPG system</li>
          <li><strong>Dedicated D&D 5E support</strong> - Built-in character sheets and complete SRD</li>
          <li><strong>Private campaign environments</strong> - Wyrlds keep your campaigns organized and secure</li>
          <li><strong>Simple and fast</strong> - No bloat, just the tools you need</li>
          <li><strong>Community-focused</strong> - Built by players, for players</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <br>

      <section>
        <h2>Get Started</h2>
        <p>
          Ready to start your adventure? <a href="/register">Create a free account</a> or
          <a href="/resources">explore our resources</a> to learn more.
        </p>
      </section>

